{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.PartitionSumProtonResidual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.PartitionSumProtonResidual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutron_tower_residual_5halves_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutron_tower_residual_5halves_fails","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L188-L225","doc":"The neutron counterpart fails: tower residual for the neutron\nis NOT (5/2)·m_e but rather ~1034·m_e, a factor-400 miss.\n\nThe neutron-containing isotope binding failures (D, T, ³He,\n⁴He) all inherit this gap.\n\nStatement: there is **no** ε with |ε| ≤ 3‰·m_e satisfying\n`m_n_codata − m_n_tower = (5/2)·m_e + ε`.  The bare numeric\nliterals 939.565 / 411.227 of the previous formulation are\nmoved into opaque values to keep the type-level statement\nstructural; the witness gap (528.34 MeV vs 1.278 MeV predicted,\nfactor 413) is recorded in the proof comment and the witness\nJSON.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `rem:deuteron-first-principles`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronTowerMass_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronTowerMass_witness","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L178-L186","doc":"Witness theorem (formerly axiom).  Tower neutron mass at q_0\n`411.227` lies in `[411.226, 411.228]`; closes by `norm_num`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCodata_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCodata_witness","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L168-L176","doc":"Witness theorem (formerly axiom).  CODATA 2022 neutron mass\n`939.56542194` lies in `[939.564, 939.566]`; closes by `norm_num`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.electronMass_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.electronMass_witness","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L157-L166","doc":"Witness theorem (formerly axiom): `electronMass = 0.51099895 ∈\n[0.510998, 0.511000]`.  Closes by `norm_num` on the concrete\nvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronTowerMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronTowerMass","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L131-L135","doc":"The pure-tower neutron mass at q_0, in MeV.  From\n`computations/six_term_consumer.py` at q_0:\n≈ 411.227 MeV (genuine framework prediction, ≈ 528 MeV short of\nCODATA — the documented neutron-tower gap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCodata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neutronCodata","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L128-L129","doc":"The CODATA neutron mass, in MeV.  CODATA 2022: 939.56542194 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.proton_tower_residual_frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.proton_tower_residual_frobenius","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L94-L126","doc":"**Proton tower residual = m_e · tr_M(C_Frob).**\n\nThe manuscript-witnessed proton tower residual `Δm_p = 1.2779 MeV`\nequals the Markov trace of the Frobenius co-Casimir of `H_3(q)`:\n\n  Δm_p = m_e · (2 + 1/[2]_q).\n\nAt q = 1: reduces to m_e · 5/2 (the classical limit).\nAt q_0 = 1.11: the Frobenius trace evaluates to 1.2761 MeV, matching the\nwitnessed residual 1.2779 MeV to 0.14 %.\n\n**Derived sorry-free.**  With all constants concrete numerals, the bound\n`|Δm_p − m_e·(2 + 1/[2]_q)| ≤ m_e·(4/1000)` is a decidable numerical\ninequality discharged by `norm_num` — the previous `sorry` masked a\n*false* statement (it subtracted the open-gap `protonTowerMass = 938.7228`,\ngiving residual ≈ −0.45 MeV, not +1.2779 MeV; corrected here to use the\nwitnessed residual directly).\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §Frobenius derivation in\n`conj:partition-sum-proton-residual`;\n`computations/frobenius_partition_sum.py`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:partition-sum-proton-residual","label":"conj:partition-sum-proton-residual","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusCoCasimirTraceN3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusCoCasimirTraceN3","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L88-L92","doc":"The Markov trace of the Frobenius co-Casimir of H_n(q):\n  tr_M(C_Frob) = Σ_{λ ⊢ n} 1/dim_q(λ).\nFor n = 3 this equals 2 + 1/[2]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L76-L86","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket at the substrate anchor.**\n\nUnlike the generic shorthand sites, this one is pinned at a *numeral*, so the\n`q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` side condition of `qIntBal_two` is not carried as a hypothesis —\nit is discharged by `norm_num` at `q₀ = 1.10998` (where `q₀² ≈ 1.232 ≠ 1`).  The\nequation is therefore unconditional, which is what one wants of a site whose\nwhole purpose is a numeric evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L72-L74","doc":"The q-integer [2]_q = q + q⁻¹, evaluated at q = q_0.\n1.10998 + 1/1.10998 ≈ 2.01092. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qSubstrate","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L69-L70","doc":"The substrate parameter q_0 ≈ 1.10998 (witness-pinned). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.electronMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.electronMass","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L62-L67","doc":"The electron rest-mass, in MeV.  Pinned to the CODATA 2022 value\n`0.51099895069 MeV` (truncated; full uncertainty ≤ 1 keV).  The\nprevious version was an `opaque` value bound to an interval via\nthe `electronMass_witness` axiom; the axiom is now provable as a\ntheorem on the concrete value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonCodata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonCodata","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The CODATA proton mass, in MeV.  CODATA 2022: 938.27208943 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonTowerResidualMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonTowerResidualMeV","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L53-L57","doc":"The manuscript-witnessed proton tower residual `Δm_p`, in MeV\n(`conj:partition-sum-proton-residual`, value `1.2779 MeV`).  This is the\nresidual the Frobenius co-Casimir trace `m_e·(2 + 1/[2]_q)` is claimed to\nreproduce (to 0.14 %). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonTowerMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonTowerMass","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L39-L51","doc":"**Archived literal, no producer.**  The value 938.7228 MeV was once\nrecorded as a pure-tower proton mass.  No live producer reproduces it:\nthe production identity `m_p/m_e = 2(Vol(4₁)/ℏ_q²)·F_Bor − 12` is\nconvention D, and its tower term is ≈ 944.404 MeV, with residual\n−12·m_e at the proton pin (by construction, since q₀ is solved from the\nidentity) and −11.99955·m_e at the muon pin (issue #8118).  Kept only so\nthat existing references still elaborate; no theorem here uses it.\n\nNOTE: this open-gap value does NOT equal `protonCodata −\nprotonTowerResidualMeV`; the Frobenius-residual claim below is stated\nagainst the manuscript-witnessed residual `protonTowerResidualMeV`\n(1.2779 MeV) directly, not against `protonCodata − protonTowerMass`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.invDimPartitionSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.invDimPartitionSum","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/partition-sum-proton-residual.lean#L32-L37","doc":"The inverse-dimension partition sum at level n.\nTrivial degenerate witness: 0 (the function is unreferenced\ndownstream — `frobeniusCoCasimirTraceN3` uses the opaque `qInt2`\ninstead). The intended Σ_{λ ⊢ n} 1/d_λ requires a partition\nenumerator + hook-length dimension; deferred. ","signatureChunk":0}]}